  "market_context": "The analyst analyzed the US Dollar Currency Index on the 4-hour chart, identifying major swing points to draw horizontal zones representing historical support and resistance areas where price reacted multiple times.",
  "key_observation": "The analyst observed four distinct price zones: a top swing high zone, two mid-level rejection zones, and a bottom support zone—each drawn to encompass candle closes and wicks for robust S/R definition.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identify the top swing high and draw a horizontal zone covering the candle closes and wicks at that level.",
    "Step 2: Move down to the next significant level and draw a second zone using the same zone-drawing method.",
    "Step 3: Locate two prior rejections in the middle of the chart and draw a third zone encompassing those reaction points.",
    "Step 4: Identify the bottom swing low and draw a fourth zone at that support level, completing the clean S/R layout."
  ],
  "outcome": null,
  "lessons": "Drawing S/R as zones—not single lines—improves accuracy by accounting for price wicks and closes; a clean multi-zone map reveals high-probability reaction areas for future entries.",
